@startuml
title ioScope Scenario View
autonumber

actor User
participant "controller.py\nscope-qt" as Bootstrap
participant ioQtScopeWindow as Window
participant ioOscilloscopeController as Controller
participant ioOscilloscopeModel as Model
participant ioWaveformGenerator as Generator
participant ioFilterPipeline as Pipeline
participant ioCompactOscilloscopeView as Compact
participant ioDetailedOscilloscopeView as Detailed

User -> Bootstrap : python controller.py scope-qt
Bootstrap -> Window : create host window with two concrete view instances
Bootstrap -> Controller : create controller with the same views
Window -> Controller : setActiveView("compact")
User -> Window : choose source / scale / offset
Window -> Controller : setInputSource(...), setScale(...), setOffset(...)
Controller -> Model : update control state
User -> Window : start acquisition
Window -> Controller : start()
Controller -> Model : refreshSamples()
Model -> Generator : generate(control_state)
Generator --> Model : raw signal
Model -> Pipeline : process(raw signal)
Pipeline --> Model : processed signal
Controller -> Compact : render(ioRenderState)
Controller -> Detailed : render(ioRenderState)
Window -> Window : show active concrete view instance
Compact --> User : compact UI updated
Detailed --> User : detailed UI updated

note over Window, Detailed
Strict MVC interpretation:
the controller renders both concrete views.
The Qt window only hosts and switches them.
end note
@enduml
